cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "ConnecTorch: compile biological connectomes into trainable PyTorch networks"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it, and cite the connectome dataset separately."
type: software
authors:
  - name: "ConnecTorch contributors"
repository-code: "https://github.com/connectorch/connectorch"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  ConnecTorch compiles an arbitrary biological wiring diagram into a sparse,
  differentiable torch.nn.Module whose topology is fixed under gradient descent.
  It provides a dataset-agnostic connectome intermediate representation, loaders
  for published connectomes including the Janelia MaleCNS v1.0 dataset, and
  gather-scatter and sparse matrix multiplication backends that never
  materialise a dense N-by-N adjacency.
references:
  - type: article
    title: "Sexual dimorphism in the complete connectome of the Drosophila male central nervous system"
    authors:
      - family-names: Berg
        given-names: Stuart
    year: 2025
    doi: 10.1101/2025.10.09.680999
    notes: "The MaleCNS v1.0 dataset this software loads and samples. Cite this separately when you use the data."
  - type: article
    title: "Connectome-constrained networks predict neural activity across the fly visual system"
    authors:
      - family-names: Lappalainen
        given-names: Janne K.
    year: 2024
    doi: 10.1038/s41586-024-07939-3
    notes: "Prior work that established connectome-constrained training."
keywords:
  - connectome
  - pytorch
  - computational neuroscience
  - sparse neural networks
